{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "242c1e6b-c18e-806e-8333-82283137d84f",
  "created_at": "2026-03-02T15:08:15-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nelson Furtado",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T14:59:41-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T14:59:48-05:00",
      "duration": 32,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah. I'm calling about a drainage problem. First, there's a puddle across about half the road in front of my place that will not go down. Second, it hasn't rained since, what, last Monday? So that's a week. And third, I'd like to know when somebody's coming to look at it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:00:20-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, a week of standing water with no rain, that's not right. Where are you located?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:00:30-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "417 Kay Street. Up on the Hill, Historic Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:00:36-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "417 Kay Street. Got it. And is the puddle right at the curb, or out in the middle of the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:00:49-05:00",
      "duration": 27,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so, first, it starts at the curb by the storm drain. Second, it spreads out toward the middle, so cars have to swing around it. Third, it's just sitting there. It's not even a fast leak or anything, it's just full and stagnant."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:01:16-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So the drain's probably clogged up or something's blocked underneath. Is there debris sitting on the grate, leaves, sand, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:01:30-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, there's stuff. [pause] Sorry, hang on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:01:35-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, Nana, I'm on the phone with the city! It's fine!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:01:42-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[crosstalk] You're all set, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:01:47-05:00",
      "duration": 40,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry. My grandmother lives with us and she's calling out from the other room, she wants to know who I'm talking to. Anyway. Yes, there's debris. First, a lot of grit and gravel built up around the grate. Second, some leaves packed in. Third, the sidewalk is a sheet of mud and grit, like you can't walk on it without tracking it all in the house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:02:27-05:00",
      "duration": 31,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that sounds like the drain's been silting up and it's pushing sediment out onto the sidewalk. I'm writing this down. Standing water at the storm drain, 417 Kay Street, no recent rain, mud and grit on the sidewalk. Anything else, like a smell or a sinkhole or the road sagging?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:02:58-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No sinkhole. No smell really. Just the water and the mud. It's annoying, honestly. I walk through it every morning to get to my car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:03:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Have you called about this before, or is this the first report?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:03:23-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I haven't called. First, I figured the landlord would handle it, second, it's the street, so it's not his, and third, I assumed somebody from the city would notice. Nobody has."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:03:42-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. It's a street drain, so it's ours. I'll put in a work order for a crew to check the catch basin and clean it out. They'll probably need the vacuum truck for that if it's packed with silt."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:04:06-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Do the crews work on weekends? Because if it's going to be next week, I'd rather know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:04:18-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mostly it's weekdays for routine stuff like this. Weekend crews are generally for emergencies. This one would go in the regular queue, so likely a few days, depending on how backed up they are."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:04:39-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A few days. Okay. So first, that means not today, second, probably not this week if it's busy, and third, I should just keep walking through the mud."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:04:56-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] I can't promise a day, I'll be honest. I can flag it as standing water with no rain so it doesn't get lost, though. Does it look like it's getting worse, or is it about the same?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:19-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "About the same. Maybe a little bigger than Thursday. The water's kind of brownish."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:28-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I'll note that it's growing. And what's a good number for you, in case the crew has a question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:41-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0176."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:43-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-six. And your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:48-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nelson Furtado. F-U-R-T-A-D-O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:51-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Nelson. Are you the owner there or renting?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:05:58-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Renting. First floor and second, we've got the whole house, my grandmother and me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:06:07-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. I'll put it in as a request from a resident at 417 Kay. If the crew gets there and can't clear it, they might send someone else out to look at the pipe."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:06:29-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. That's fine. As long as somebody actually looks at it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:06:36-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hold on, one second. [pause] She says hello to you. She says the water was there before Christmas too, but I don't think that's true, I think it's just since the last big thaw."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:06:57-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tell her hello back. Either way, I'll note it's been sitting a while. If it's a drain that's been silting up for weeks, that tells the crew something."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:07:14-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So first, you've got my address, second, you've got my number, and third, you're putting it in the queue."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:07:27-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. If it's still sitting there after a few days, call back and mention the work order. I'll give you a reference when I submit it. Hang on a second."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:07:46-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:07:48-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Okay, it's in. I don't have a specific date, but it's logged as standing water, no rain, sediment on the sidewalk. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:08:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Thanks, Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:08:07-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it, Nelson. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-02T15:08:13-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too."
    }
  ],
